  "details": "There appear to be two issues with Bloom in the current version of Post Processing Stack v2.\n\nThe first one is this issue, where player capsules and the loading man avatar have weird reflections on them: https://i.imgur.com/XWaHPNK.png\n\nThe second bug happens on all objects with intense bloom. I created a sphere that is intentionally very bloomy, but the bloom seems to be cut off in a strange way. I made the sphere solid white, but it has the same odd reflections as the player capsules do: https://i.imgur.com/YlmE8UO.jpg\n\nOne map where this happens is \"Rokk's Avatar Village\", with world ID: wrld_5045bf89-96a6-4e00-b975-4c15d11a0e25\n\nThere is a UI panel near spawn that allows you to turn the Post Processing off, whjch immediately stops these bugs from happening.",
